<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  OpenArm v2 bimanual — hand-reviewed self-collision exemptions.

  This SRDF exists ONLY to carry deliberate ACM exemptions into the MJCF
  collision lowering (`openral collision lower`, source: mjcf). The sweep can
  auto-disable a pair only when it collides in EVERY sampled pose; these pairs
  do NOT, so each one is a reviewed judgment recorded here, the same explicit
  channel URDF robots use, instead of hand edits to the generated ACM block.

  Re-measured 2026-09-24 against the geometry fitted to the MJCF meshes
  (`openral collision lower`, hazard-log Entry 045),
  over seeded in-limit poses:
    primitives - the kernel collision model, kernel_predicates.shape_distance, 2000 poses
    meshes     - the MJCF collision meshes, openral_hal.convex_distance (certified
                 GJK/SAT; every result certified), 1500 poses. Not mj_geomDistance:
                 under MuJoCo 3.8.0 native CCD returns false zeros and libccd false
                 overlaps on these very pairs (libccd put link5/link7 at 38% overlap).

                         primitives                meshes: min clearance
    link1<->link3        overlap 62%, rest +12 mm  14.8 mm
    finger_pair<->link5  overlap ~70%, rest -28 mm 16.1 mm
    finger_pair<->link6  overlap 100%, rest -37 mm 23.8 mm
    link5<->link7        overlap ~68%, rest +25 mm 2.9 mm (1st percentile 3.0 mm)

  The meshes of every pair here never touch; one primitive per link cannot
  separate them. link5<->link7 is the thin one: the wrist housings either side
  of link6 pass within 3 mm, but the flat floor (min 2.9 / p1 3.0 mm) is the
  wrist geometry, not sampling luck. It was exempt on master too
  (always-colliding under the old capsules).

  RETIRED 2026-09-25 (PR #324, docs/reference/collision-geometry-review.md §11):
  link1<->link3 on both arms. Both links now lower to a box plus their exact
  convex hull (tight_geometry), and the kernel re-asks the pair of the two
  hulls; the hulls are 12.1 mm apart at their closest over 500 seeded in-limit
  poses and +16.6 mm at rest, so the pair is CHECKED again instead of exempted.
  The retired rows only ever removed a check; putting one back needs the same
  WG sign-off as any other row here.
  SAFETY (CLAUDE.md §3): every row here REDUCES what the kernel checks and
  needs safety-WG sign-off to change.
-->
<robot name="openarm">
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_left_finger_pair" link2="openarm_left_link5" reason="Meshes never closer than 16.3 mm (1500 certified poses); fitted primitives overlap at rest (d=-0.028 m)."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_right_finger_pair" link2="openarm_right_link5" reason="Meshes never closer than 16.1 mm (1500 certified poses); fitted primitives overlap at rest (d=-0.028 m)."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_left_finger_pair" link2="openarm_left_link6" reason="Meshes never closer than 23.8 mm (1500 certified poses); fitted primitives overlap in every pose."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_right_finger_pair" link2="openarm_right_link6" reason="Meshes never closer than 23.8 mm (1500 certified poses); fitted primitives overlap in every pose."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_left_link5" link2="openarm_left_link7" reason="Wrist housings either side of link6: meshes never closer than 2.9 mm (1500 certified poses, 1st percentile 3.0 mm); fitted primitives overlap in 67%. Exempt on master too."/>
  <disable_collisions link1="openarm_right_link5" link2="openarm_right_link7" reason="Wrist housings either side of link6: meshes never closer than 2.9 mm (1500 certified poses, 1st percentile 3.0 mm); fitted primitives overlap in 69%. Exempt on master too."/>
</robot>
